  "question": {
    "text": "Experimentally it was found that a metal oxide has formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>0.98</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. Metal M, is present as <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> in its oxide. Fraction of the metal which exists as <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> would be:",
