  "solution": {
    "text": "Consider one mole of the oxide, then<br /><br />Moles of M = 0.98;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Moles of O<sup>2-&nbsp;</sup>= 1<br /><br />Let &#39;x&#39; moles of M are in +3 oxidation state, then Moles of M<sup>2+</sup> = 0.98-x<br /><br />On doing charge balancing we get&nbsp;<br /><br />(0.98 - x)2 + 3x&nbsp; = 2<br /><br />Or 1.96 - 2x + 3x - 2 = 0<br /><br />Or x = 0.04<br /><br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756; %</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.04</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.98</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.08</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math>",
    "image": null
